<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The RichOS iPhone app's privacy manifest (required by App Store Connect since 2024-05-01).

  REQUIRED-REASON APIs: none. The Release app and both extensions call no API in Apple's
  required-reason list (file timestamps, system boot time, disk space, active keyboards,
  UserDefaults). That is measured, not assumed: `Release/check-release.sh` scans every Release
  Mach-O's symbols for each category and fails if one appears that is not declared here. The
  preserved app declared two (file timestamps C617.1, disk space E174.1); this app does not store
  recordings by date or check free space, so it has neither. Add a category here in the same
  commit as the code that needs it; the check will refuse the build otherwise.

  COLLECTED DATA ("collect" = sent off the phone and kept by us or a partner longer than the
  request needs; developer.apple.com/app-store/app-privacy-details). Messages, voice, photos and
  files go to the person's own Mac and are not collected by us. What the hosted RichOS Connect
  service keeps to deliver reply notifications: the phone's push token and a hash of its device
  key (Device ID). It is not linked to a person (there are no accounts) or used for tracking.

  NO DIAGNOSTICS. The deployed Connect Worker keeps none: its schema has five tables (hosts,
  nonces, allowed_hosts, push_bindings, push_jobs; `richos/mobile/service/connect/schema.sql`),
  jobs expire within one hour, and logs, traces, Logpush and tail consumers are disabled
  (`richos/mobile/service/notifications.md`). The seven-day diagnostics once declared here came
  from a PRD proposal that was never built. `NotificationService/Tests/main.swift` P1-P4 fail if
  the manifest and that schema drift apart.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeDeviceID</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
